🔔 Updated: I want to call attention to the #polio epidemics happening in #sudan and #🍉 

I remember when I was younger in Sudan around 10 years old and polio was everywhere especially with our #houseless and #orphans it’s a devastating sight to behold. 

There’s one moment that’s forever etched into my memory, a young boy who lost everything from the waist below with flip flops on his hand drinking dirty water on the ground because no one would come near him to offer clean water fearing the contagious disease. I was too young to understand or wrap my mind around that moment. 

I created this carousel with him in mind, I was too scared to bring him water but I can at least try to educate and fundraise now. 

There’s no cure only vaccines which means if they are not given the proper care they need the only alternative is for them to lose limbs or be taken away by it. And even if they survive the suffering doesn’t end. 

Both areas have next to no medical facilities, both areas have rampant famine, no clean water, no access which means that this has the potential to spread widely and quickly. Please keep your eyes on this and support grassroots orgs who are caring for our dear children. 

