⚡️Major announcement for us—after twelve years of community-led collaborative design for new systems and new cultures, we have never not once taken the time to host a Gala for ourselves. We are a different kind of non-profit organization, mainly because we are a public service and supported by all of you. Our team and work has grown in impact and responsibility. 

🌊 What @celinecelines and @collisbrowne started in 2012 based on digital literacy for climate & human rights has filled a huge gap for Media Justice and Systems Change with a beautiful collective team:

@prae_rae 🖍️
@yallahbackgirl ✏️
@afeefness 🔍
@dal333n 🗝️
@yassayassayassa 🎀
@joshuaphillll 🔭
🌀

The majority of Slow Factory are people of the Global South and we are here to shake things up, shift the narrative, change culture and transform harmful systems to replace expired ones built on the blueprint of colonialism and racism. We know we can design so much better than that because we always have. We got this!

🪬 This year, the stakes are higher, we need to gather behind closed doors, raise funds to do so much more. Build spaces in our communities, share knowledge and build power. We only have each other. 

🩸 War criminals raise millions to continue oppressing us while we try so hard to make ends meet. This scarcity mindset for collective care & liberation ends now. We call on you all to fund the revolution and change the way you want to live.

Join us. ❤️ And if you can’t make it in person, please consider becoming a monthly supporter. Your contribution fuels what we are all working towards: collective care & liberation 🌀

