It’s a “love the culture” kinda day. 

I have some questions for you! 

Where are you from (in the words of @amerzahr “from from”)? 

Has there been a point in your life where you distanced yourself from your heritage because of shame/embarrassment/being made fun of/you hated feeling different from everyone else around you? 

If so (and even if not!) - what has helped you connect with your people and homeland? 

For me it was learning about the history of Palestinians as an indigenous people. I find a lot inspiration from #NativeTikTok & #IndigenousTikTok. I so admire how they honor their ancestors in everything they do. And seeing my own family’s history in connection with other indigenous groups around the world (especially those in the U.S. and Canada) was a game changer for me. I’m grateful for their content and inspiration to dive deeper into my lineage every day. ✊🏽

Some of my favorite accounts if you aren’t following yet are: 

@haatepah 
@modern_warrior__ 
@shinanova 
@tiamiscihk 
@marikasila 
@indigenous_baddie 

